-- title:
--   Étale coordinate on the stalk at a good off-branch point, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, write $\bar F$ for `fieldBar q M'`, that is for `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ obtained by base change of the level-$\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ function field, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the unit-group reduction map of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ given by `dvd_sq_mul q M'`; write $\bar E$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field; and write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   *Base data.* A prime $q$ together with the hypothesis $q = 3$, a level $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$, with `hW` asserting that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' κ`, the set of places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen}) \in$ `ssJSet q κ`.
--
--   *Reduction data.* The inclusion `hle` of $\bar E$ in $\bar F$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ on $\bar E$ with residue field target `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`; and `hR₀`, which asserts for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\bar E$ that this image lies in $R_0$.`integers` and that its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *Component rings.* An index $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   *Igusa hypotheses.* `hIg_inf` identifies $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathtt{lineInfty } q)$ as the Gauss ring: $f$ belongs to it precisely when there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ non-zero and $f\cdot y = x$ after coefficientwise inclusion of $A$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. `hIg` says that every line is reached from `lineInfty q` by some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q` equal to it and with the corresponding ring the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathtt{lineInfty } q)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`. `hIg_inj` requires $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ injective, and `hIg_perm` that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family.
--
--   *Supersingular hypotheses.* `hSS_A` says that for $s \in W$ an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ precisely when it lies in $A$. `hSS_over` says, for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0$.`integers` having non-negative order at every place of $\bar E$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the class of `coeffEmb _ jq` has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and of $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$. `hSS_fix` requires each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ to be invariant under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   *The prolongation.* A regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on $\bar F$ with residue field target `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, with `hR` asserting $R$.`integers` $= O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathtt{lineInfty } q)$, and `hR₀O` asserting that $f \in R_0$.`integers` holds exactly when the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathtt{lineInfty } q)$.
--
--   *Constants.* An element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$. A subfield $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field, together with `hκ`: every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. Further, a prime $\ell \geq 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *One finite layer.* An intermediate field $K_1$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, finite over $k_0$, and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ with $A_1 = A \cap K_1$, which is a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The field $\bar F$ carries the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$. The conclusion is then a statement about every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0$ in $\bar F$ satisfying four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\bar F$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ finite over $k_0$, any finite family $c_i \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and any family $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$ satisfying $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ has all $a_i = 0$; and every element of $\bar F$ whose Laurent expansion has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb`) belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $\bar F$ generated by the image of $K_1$. Given an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map agrees on $A_1$ with the inclusion $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$, and an element $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in $\bar F$ is the class of the $q$-expansion `coeffEmb _ jq` of the modular invariant, with $j_1 \neq 0$, let $\mathfrak X_1 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the two-chart integral model, the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` and $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf` attached to $j_1$ and $j_1^{-1}$.
--
--   Five predicates on points $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ are introduced. `InStalk x f`, for $f \in T_1$: for every point $y$ of `XFin` mapping to $x$ under `ιFin` there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for `XInf`, `ιInf` and `chartAlgInf`. `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$ in both charts. `Centred P x`, for a place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: $P$ is rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ exactly when `InMax x f`; this predicate does not occur in the implication asserted below. `GoodPt x`: the image of $x$ under `toBase` is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ is closed, in the sense that $x \rightsquigarrow y$ forces $y = x$; in either chart, every chart element whose image in $\bar F$ is a non-unit of $R$.`integers` lies in every prime of that chart lying over $x$; and for every point $y$ of `XFin` over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`. `Reads x Q`, for a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over $\kappa$: every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in $R$.`integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and that residue is a non-unit there exactly when `InMax x f`. `OffBranch x`: for every point of the projective line other than `lineInfty q`, and for every prime $y$ of either chart lying over $x$, there is a chart element $b \notin y$ whose image in $\bar F$ is a non-unit of the corresponding ring $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of that line.
--
--   The assertion is: for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ and every place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over $\kappa$ such that `GoodPt x`, `OffBranch x` and `Reads x Q` hold, there exist a subring $S$ of $\bar F$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon A_1[X] \to S$ and a ring homomorphism $\chi \colon S \to \kappa$ with the following properties.
--
--   First, $S$ is the stalk read inside $\bar F$: an element $f$ of $\bar F$ lies in $S$ precisely when $f$ lies in $T_1$ and satisfies `InStalk x f`. Second, $\chi$ cuts out the maximal ideal of that stalk: for $f \in S$ one has $\chi(f) = 0$ precisely when $f$, viewed in $T_1$, satisfies `InMax x f`. Third, the map sending $a \in A_1$ to the residue in $\kappa$ of $a$ viewed in $A$ is surjective. Fourth, the image in $\bar F$ of every $a \in A_1$ lies in $S$; fifth, $\varphi(C\,a)$ is that image for every $a \in A_1$; sixth, $\chi(\varphi(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; seventh, $\chi(\varphi(X)) = 0$. Eighth, $S$ is a local ring with $\ker \chi$ its maximal ideal. Ninth, $\varphi$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type. Tenth, every $f \in T_1$ is a ratio of elements of $S$: there are $g,h \in S$ with $h \neq 0$ and $f h = g$ in $\bar F$. Eleventh, every element of $S$ lies in $R$.`integers`, and, for every generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A_1$ and every $f \in S$, the element $f$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R$.`integers` if and only if $\varphi(C\,\varpi)$ divides $f$ in $S$. Twelfth, for every $f \in S$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue in the residue field of $Q$ equals the image of $\chi(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q$.`ResidueField`. Thirteenth, $\varphi(X)$ lies in $R$.`integers` and its $R$-residue has $Q$-order equal to $1$.
--
--   This is the local step, at a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model lying on the $\infty$-Igusa component and away from the supersingular $j$-invariants, which presents the stalk there as an étale $A_1[X]$-algebra with residue character factoring through the residue field of $A$, the coordinate $X$ becoming a uniformiser at the place $Q$ read by the regular prolongation $R$. It is the $q = 3$ case of this per-point statement, and it feeds the construction of the smooth Igusa base model in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three).
